QED v2 desirability coefficients (qed_v2_coefficients.json) — CC-BY-SA-3.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The QED v2 desirability-function coefficients are refit on the ChEMBL 35 set of
approved oral small-molecule drugs, replacing the original Bickerton 2012
coefficients. Because they are derived from ChEMBL data, they are distributed
under CC-BY-SA 3.0 (ShareAlike, attribution required), with attribution to:

  ChEMBL — CC-BY-SA 3.0. EMBL-EBI, https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/

The QED method itself (Asymmetric Double Sigmoidal desirability functions) is from:

  Bickerton, G.R., Paolini, G.V., Besnard, J., Muresan, S., Hopkins, A.L.
  "Quantifying the chemical beauty of drugs." Nat. Chem. 4, 90-98 (2012).
